loom_public_page('About LOOM','LOOM is a modular application engine designed around inspectable capabilities, project-scoped composition, durable identity, and replaceable core releases.',
'<section class="card"><h2>Modular by design</h2><p>LOOM discovers modules through manifests, keeps user-facing actions inspectable through the Action Registry, and lets project-owned identity and content remain separate from the replaceable engine.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Projects stay projects</h2><p>Each project can inherit LOOM defaults and override only what it needs. Instance Projects and installation state live outside normal release replacement so core updates do not erase project-owned data.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Built for humans and automation</h2><p>LOOM surfaces capabilities, settings, actions, permissions, and project boundaries in structured forms so both people and software agents can understand what they are changing.</p></section>','about');
